<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Which devices DacAttachActivity is offered.

  Class 1 is audio, subclass 1 is the audio *control* interface — the one that owns the volume.
  No vendor or product id, deliberately: the Apple adapter is the one that was measured, but the
  bug is a host that never sets a standard control, so every adapter with a quiet power-on default
  has it. A vendor list would fix this for one part number and for nothing anybody else plugs in.

  Matching a class rather than a device means this is offered speakers, interfaces and headsets
  too. Being offered one costs an invisible activity and a handful of control transfers; the user
  is asked once per device and can say no, and nothing here writes to a device that reports no
  volume control. Note that a device is only ever offered while the feature is switched on: the
  activity is declared disabled and enabled from DacUnlock.setEnabled.
-->
<resources>
    <usb-device class="1" subclass="1" />
</resources>
